        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe media-generation model-ref module exposes a redundant named type for the same provider/model shape already owned by `ProviderModelRef`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReturn `ProviderModelRef` directly from `parseGenerationModelRef` and remove the unused alias. This keeps one canonical type without changing runtime behavior or supported plugin SDK entrypoints.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Internal model-reference typing has one fewer duplicate name.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/media-generation-core/src/model-ref.test.ts` — 5 tests passed.\n- `corepack pnpm --filter @openclaw/media-generation-core build` — passed on Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox (`tbx_01kwq90wnvc6nf78e34sgybe4v`, Actions run `28716902914`).\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main --prompt-file /tmp/model-ref-alias-review-evidence.md --stream-engine-output` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
